# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Yard Studio — frontend environment variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` (or configure on Vercel project settings) to enable
# the flags below for your environment.

# --- API base (production / preview / special setups) ---
# Local `npm run dev`: leave VITE_API_URL **unset** (or comment it out). The app
# will call same-origin `/api/...` (e.g. http://localhost:5173/api/...) and
# `vite.config.ts` proxies that to http://localhost:3002 — no browser CORS to 3002.
#
# Only set VITE_API_URL if the browser must talk to the API host directly, e.g.:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://theyardapis.01tech.work/api
# Then your backend must allow CORS for this frontend origin (e.g. localhost:5173).
#
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3002/api

# --- Payment return URL (usually leave unset) ---
# Checkout sends window.location.origin to the API so Stripe returns to the same host
# (localhost:5173, Vercel preview, or production domain). Only set if you must override:
# VITE_APP_PUBLIC_URL=https://theyard.01tech.work

# Demo / mock mode is disabled — the app always uses the backend API.
# VITE_DEMO_MODE is ignored if set.
